  "reference_solution": "WITH active AS (SELECT DISTINCT account_id FROM events WHERE event_type='export' AND event_at>=TIMESTAMP '2026-09-01' AND event_at<TIMESTAMP '2026-10-01') SELECT COUNT(*) AS eligible_accounts,COUNT(active.account_id) AS activated_accounts,COUNT(active.account_id)*1.0/NULLIF(COUNT(*),0) AS activation_rate FROM accounts a LEFT JOIN active USING(account_id) WHERE a.is_internal IS FALSE",
  "solution_explanation": "Drive the denominator from eligible accounts. Reduce activity to distinct accounts, preserve non-active accounts, and protect the zero denominator.",
  "hints": [
    "The unit of analysis is an account, not an event.",
    "Calculate eligibility independently of observed activity.",
    "Join distinct qualifying account IDs to the eligible population and use a safe fractional ratio."
  ],
  "senior_review": "The definition explicitly identifies population, action, time window, entity and zero behavior. A model cannot reward unstated alternate definitions.",
